/-!
# Stalks of the analytification

Let `X` be a scheme of finite type over `ℂ`, `X^an` its analytification and `α_X : X^an → X`
the comparison morphism. This file proves the basic properties of the analytification.

1. `α_X` is continuous; it identifies the points of `X^an` with the closed points of `X`; and at
   a point `y` of a chart `Spec ℂ[z₁, …, zₙ]/I` with coordinates `p`, the stalk
   `𝒪_{X^an,y}` is `ℂ{z - p}/I ℂ{z - p}`.
2. The stalk map `φ : 𝒪_{X,y} → 𝒪_{X^an,y}` of `α_X` is a faithfully flat local homomorphism
   inducing isomorphisms `𝒪_{X,y}/𝔪^N ≅ 𝒪_{X^an,y}/𝔪^N` on all finite jets.
3. `(F^an)_y = 𝒪_{X^an,y} ⊗_{𝒪_{X,y}} F_y`; `F ↦ F^an` is exact, commutes with tensor
   products (through the isomorphism `(F ⊗ G)^an ≅ F^an ⊗ G^an` sending `s ⊗ t` to
   `s ⊗ t`) and preserves invertible sheaves; and a finite type `𝒪_X`-module with `F^an = 0`
   vanishes.
4. The comparison maps `c^q` are natural for every pair `(φ, ψ)` of maps of abelian sheaves
   `φ : F → G`, `ψ : F^an → G^an` with `ψ ∘ ι_F = ι_G ∘ α_X⁻¹ φ`; they commute with the
   connecting maps of short exact sequences of `𝒪_X`-modules; and on `𝒪_X`-modules `(c^q)_{q ≥ 0}`
   is the only morphism of δ-functors `H^q(X, -) ⟶ H^q(X^an, (-)^an)` extending `c^0`.
5. For a closed immersion `i : X → P` into a scheme `P` of finite type over `ℂ`, `i^an` is a
   closed embedding, the analytic local rings of `X` are those of `P` modulo the ideal of `X`,
   `i^an` underlies a map of ringed spaces `θ : 𝒪_{P^an} ⟶ i^an_* 𝒪_{X^an}` compatible with `i^#`,
   the adjunction map `(i_* F)^an ⟶ i^an_* F^an` is an isomorphism, and under the identifications
   `H^q(P, i_* F) ≅ H^q(X, F)` and `H^q(P^an, (i_* F)^an) ≅ H^q(X^an, F^an)` (pullback along `i`,
   resp. `i^an`, followed by the counit, resp. the adjoint of the adjunction map) the comparison
   maps of `i_* F` and `F` agree.

## Main results

* `MMP.Analytic.analytification_stalks`: the five statements above.

## Implementation notes

* "Of finite type" is `LocallyOfFiniteType` together with `QuasiCompact`.
* The independence of `𝒪_{X^an}` of the chart presentations and the well-definedness of
  `α_X^#` hold by construction: `MMP.Analytic.analytification` glues over all charts at once.
* The chart isomorphism, the jet isomorphisms, the stalk tensor isomorphism and the stalk
  isomorphism of a closed immersion are each pinned by their value on the image of the
  algebraic stalk (`φ`, the germs of `MMP.Analytic.analytifyModuleUnit`, the stalk map of `i`).
* Exactness of `F ↦ F^an` is the preservation of finite limits and finite colimits; tensor
  products are those of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor`; an invertible sheaf is one
  locally isomorphic to the structure sheaf.
* The vanishing statement is stated for modules of finite type, which contain the coherent ones.
* The connecting maps of `H^q(T, -)` are those of the short exact sequence of total complexes of
  Godement sections `Γ(T, G^•(F[0]))`, whose homology is `MMP.Analytic.sheafCohomology`; the
  exactness of these sequences is part of the statement. A morphism of δ-functors is a family of
  natural transformations commuting with these connecting maps.
* The adjunction map of a closed immersion and `(i^an)^#` are each pinned by their values on
  algebraic sections (the units `MMP.Analytic.analytifyModuleUnit`, resp. `α^#` and `i^#`),
  which determine them since `(i_* F)^an` is generated by the image of `i_* F`.

## References

* [Serre, *Géométrie algébrique et géométrie analytique*], §2.
* [SGA 1, Exposé XII], §1.
-/

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry Topology TopologicalSpace Opposite IsLocalRing
